+# Cancellation
+
+For whoever changes how a member cancels a pantry order, or answers a member whose cancellation was refused. A member
+may cancel a pantry order until 2 hours before its pickup slot starts; after that the app refuses, and a member who
+cannot come calls the pantry, where the volunteers decide. Volunteers start packing bags 2 hours before each slot, and
+members were cancelling minutes before pickup, at 16:50 for a 17:00 slot: by 7 October 2026, 25 bags of fresh food
+had been thrown away that month, though a banner had asked members to cancel earlier since the summer.
+
+## The cutoff
+
+The cutoff is `CUTOFF` in [`larder/cancellation.py`](../../larder/cancellation.py): 2 hours, the length of the
+packing shift. A cancellation before the packing starts costs the pantry nothing; one after it costs a packed bag.
+
+`can_cancel(pickup_starts, now)` allows a cancellation only while `now` is strictly earlier than the cutoff. For a
+slot starting at 17:00:
+
+| Cancelled at | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| 14:59 | Allowed |
+| 15:00 | Refused |
+| 16:50 | Refused |
+
+## After the cutoff
+
+The app refuses the cancellation. A member who cannot come calls the pantry, and the volunteers decide what to do
+with the pantry order. The pantry asked that the refusal message give its phone number.
